Student Marks Analyzer
A beginner-friendly Python mini project that analyzes the marks of five students and displays their academic results.

Features
Takes marks as input for five students.
Stores marks in a Python list.
Counts the number of passed students (marks ≥ 40).
Counts the number of failed students (marks < 40).
Calculates total and average marks.
Finds the highest marks.
Displays the list of students' marks.

Python Concepts Used
Variables and data types
Lists and append()
for loops
if-else statements
Counters

Built-in functions: sum(), len(), and max()

User input and output

Purpose
This project helped me practice Python fundamentals, conditional logic, loops, lists, and basic data analysis.

How to Run
Install Python.
Save the code as student_marks_analyzer.py.
Run the following command:
python student_marks_analyzer.py

